## Impact

* Users can lose funds if they repay their loan after the liquidation grace period has passed.
* The NFT collateral can become stuck and cannot be withdrawn by either the user or the Stability Pool.
* Third parties who attempt to repay the debt on behalf of the user after the grace period also lose their funds.

## Tools Used

* Hardhat
* Manual Review

## Recommendations

1. **Add a Check in the** **`repay`** **Function**: Implement a check in the `repay` function to prevent users from repaying their debt after the liquidation grace period has expired. This can be done by verifying the liquidation status and the elapsed time since the liquidation started.

```solidity
function _repay(uint256 amount, address onBehalfOf) internal {
    if (amount == 0) revert InvalidAmount();
    if (onBehalfOf == address(0)) revert AddressCannotBeZero();

    UserData storage user = userData[onBehalfOf];

    // Check if the user is under liquidation and if the grace period has expired
    if (user.isUnderLiquidation && block.timestamp > user.liquidationStartTime + GRACE_PERIOD) {
        revert GracePeriodExpired();
    }

    // other code

}
```

1. Add a check in `liquidateBorrower()` and `finalizeLiquidation()` to reset liquidation status when `userDebt == 0 && user.isUnderLiquidation`. For example:

```solidity
if (userDebt == 0 && user.isUnderLiquidation) {
    isUnderLiquidation[userAddress] = false;
    liquidationStartTime[userAddress] = 0;
}
```

This prevents users from remaining in liquidation status after their debt is cleared by the user or another user and they failed to call `closeLiquidation` before the period expired.

## Summary

In `LendingPool` the functions that rely on the indexes (liquidity index, usage index) update them before executing state changes, in order to ensure they are working with accurate data. \
\
On the other hand `LendingPool::getNormalizedIncome()` method does not refresh the liquidity index, returning a stale value.

## Vulnerability Details

The liquidity index returned by `LendingPool::getNormalizedIncome()` is stale. All of the contracts that rely on this method will use stale data for performing calculations.

## Examples

* [RToken::transfer()](https://github.com/Cyfrin/2025-02-raac/blob/main/contracts/core/tokens/RToken.sol#L213)
* [RToken::\_update()](https://github.com/Cyfrin/2025-02-raac/blob/main/contracts/core/tokens/RToken.sol#L309)
* [RToken::balanceOf()](https://github.com/Cyfrin/2025-02-raac/blob/main/contracts/core/tokens/RToken.sol#L196)
* [RToken::totalSupply()](https://github.com/Cyfrin/2025-02-raac/blob/main/contracts/core/tokens/RToken.sol#L204)
* [RToken::calculateDustAmount()](https://github.com/Cyfrin/2025-02-raac/blob/main/contracts/core/tokens/RToken.sol#L319)

## Impact

Calculations in `RToken` relying on the liquidity index will be performed with stale data, leading to incorrect results.

