Consider removing these checks here and refactoring the code. Then, `_solverLock` doesn't have to be set in `reconcile()`. Note that `_solverLock` ensures that `reconcile()` is only called once; depending on the refactor, an alternative solution might be required. Access to `reconcile()` could be restricted to specific phases. Also see the issue: "Locking mechanism is complicated".

