summary:
A bug was reported in the Yieldy smart contract code, which is part of the code-423n4/2022-06-yieldy repository on GitHub. The bug was observed when a REBASE_ROLE called the rebase function with a profit of 10 and a currentTotalSupply of 90. The updatedTotalSupply was calculated as 90+10=100, but since the MAX_SUPPLY was 91, the updatedTotalSupply was updated to 91. This caused the _storeRebase function to be called with an updatedTotalSupply of 91 and a _profit of 10, which is incorrect since 10 amount from _profit was not utilized and only 1 amount was utilized. This became a problem in rebasePercent calculation, where it was calculated on the full 10 amount instead of 1.

To mitigate this issue, the code should be updated to the following:

```
if (updatedTotalSupply > MAX_SUPPLY) {
_profit=_profit - (updatedTotalSupply-MAX_SUPPLY);
                updatedTotalSupply = MAX_SUPPLY;

            }
```

This will ensure that the _profit amount is correctly utilized and that the rebasePercent is calculated on the correct amount.

