summary:
A bug has been found in the Note contract where if the `_initialSupply` is not equal to 0, then the `_totalSupply` will overflow when the `_mint_to_Accountant` function executes `_mint(msg.sender, type(uint).max)`. This bug was first reported by cccz and later found by Picodes. The code snippets associated with the bug can be found at the provided link. 

The recommended mitigation steps to fix this bug are to change the constructor code in ERC20.sol to:

```
constructor(string memory name_, string memory symbol_) public {
    _name = name_;
    _symbol = symbol_;
}
```

And in Note.sol:

```
constructor() ERC20("Note", "NOTE") {
    admin = msg.sender;
}
```

The bug was confirmed by abhipingle (Canto) and was determined to have a Medium severity. The bug was also found to be a duplicate of Issue #53 (H-06). The impact of the bug is that the Sponsor would be forced to re-deploy the contract.

